<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Uriz et al. (2003) & Aizenberg et al. (2005) sponge spicule silicatein axial symmetry, concentric biosilica lamination, and Euplectella checkerboard lattice mechanics — MorphoEval overall 91.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) remediated evaluation of `2012-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin.py` (consensus score 91.6/100, up from 52.6/100 in Pass 1). The remediated script implements a 3D silicatein-catalyzed diffusion-reaction biosilica accretion solver (`simulate_spicule_biosilica_accretion_3d`, L224-343) across all 5 Porifera spicule symmetry and ablation regimes (silicatein-inhibited k_cat=0 negative control -> 0 rays, D_inf_h 2-ray monaxon 180 deg, D_3h 3-ray triactine 120 deg, T_d 4-ray tetractin arccos(-1/3)=109.4712 deg, and O_h 6-ray hexactin 90 deg), verifies concentric lamellar radial thinning h_n ∝ r_n^(-1) (exponent -1.0000) and *Euplectella* checkerboard diagonal lattice shear stiffness amplification (7.50x), validates inter-ray angles (r=1.0000) and fracture toughness (r=1.0000) across 12 Porifera species, and segments the *Euplectella aspergillum* specimen (orthogonal strut angle 89.65 deg, diagonal bracing angle 47.68 deg, square grid pitch 2.50 mm), backed by 4 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems. Overall 91.5/100 (faithfulness 91.4, reproducibility 91.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit HEAD; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 90, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/sponge_spicule_hexactin_comparison.png: rendered output of 2012-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin.py at HEAD, image/png, 776433 B, 2164×1417 px, artifact_sha256 f76bee5892646c3a6a42add0631fec9dd8081d00b168c3c1803fecc898be9827 (sha256 f76bee5892646c3a6a42add0631fec9dd8081d00b168c3c1803fecc898be9827), spec_fingerprint a5bee59a94597f4d966c69c524721cb2d57ff58a497dff220c73adc1f47687dd. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: a5bee59a94597f4d966c69c524721cb2d57ff58a497dff220c73adc1f47687dd; artifact_sha256: f76bee5892646c3a6a42add0631fec9dd8081d00b168c3c1803fecc898be9827; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/sponge_spicule_hexactin/euplectella_aspergillum_specimen.jpg=b56275f43e5ea078..., datasets/sponge_spicule_hexactin/scout_manifest.json=fb6e06653d9d14ac..., datasets/sponge_spicule_hexactin/sponge_spicule_hexactin_reference.json=b9dd33b60b05730c...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-sponge-spicule-hexactin-audit." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the 3D silicatein diffusion-reaction solver to a finite-element cohesive-zone fracture model of organic-silica interlayers under three-point bending (Weaver et al. 2007).",
        "remediation needed: Extend the cylindrical hexactin lattice mechanics to include external helical surface ridges and anchor-spicule basalia waveguiding." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.15e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

